INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at, predicate_id)
SELECT 'BP26-PROVENANCE-MARKING-1: Machine-readable AI-provenance marking (C2PA manifests for PDFs and images, signed JSON sidecars for HTML) before 2026-12-02', 'Charter pillar: research. BP26 best-practice catalogue item 1.4, top-20 rank 2 (research report wf-232b4527-680f-8492-8dc9-5ab6ae365e14 (2026-10-26); owner directive 2026-10-26).
Project BP26.EDITORIAL under program QNFO.RSCH (program-manager:QNFO.RSCH).

PRACTICE: EU AI Act Art. 50(2): output of generative systems already on the market before 2026-08-02 must be marked in a machine-readable, detectable way by 2026-12-02 (Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 transitional rule). Attach C2PA manifests (c2pa.created, digitalSourceType trainedAlgorithmicMedia) to paper PDFs and social images; for HTML publish a signed, time-stamped JSON sidecar linked by <link rel="c2pa-manifest"> plus JSON-LD flags. Keep the X.509 signing key as a Worker secret under the secret lock with automated renewal checks.

SOURCES: C2PA 2.2 specification https://spec.c2pa.org/specifications/specifications/2.2/specs/C2PA_Specification.html; C2PA implementation guidance https://spec.c2pa.org/specifications/specifications/2.2/guidance/Guidance.html; Commission Code of Practice on marking and labelling (2026-06-10) https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/news/commission-publishes-code-practice-marking-and-labelling-ai-generated-content; Bird & Bird analysis https://www.twobirds.com/en/insights/2026/taking-the-eu-ai-act-to-practice-the-final-transparency-code-of-practice

APPLIES TO: papers.qnfo.org PDFs, social images, q08.org, reading.q08.org, ipatent drafts. Effort M.

