SELECT 'BP26-SOCIAL-AUTOMATION-1: Automated social posting within platform rules: bot labels, official APIs only, no unsolicited mentions, rate caps', 'Charter pillar: reach. BP26 best-practice catalogue item 1.9, top-20 rank 9 (research report wf-232b4527-680f-8492-8dc9-5ab6ae365e14 (2026-10-26); owner directive 2026-10-26).
Project BP26.REACH under program QNFO.REACH (program-manager:QNFO.REACH).

PRACTICE: X: Automated label on and a managing human account linked, official API only, no unsolicited @mentions or auto-replies, no automated follows or likes. Bluesky: bot self-label. Mastodon: ''This is an automated account''. LinkedIn: official API and Buffer only. Everywhere: rate caps, no bulk identical cross-posts, link the source page. Until the owner sets the account labels (identity-bound card bp26-social-bot-labels), every automated post carries a short automation marker in its text.

SOURCES: X Developer Guidelines https://docs.x.com/developer-guidelines; X automated-account labels https://help.x.com/en/using-x/automated-account-labels; X authenticity policy https://help.x.com/en/rules-and-policies/authenticity; Bluesky moderation (bot self-label) https://docs.bsky.app/docs/advanced-guides/moderation; Bluesky developer guidelines https://docs.bsky.app/docs/support/developer-guidelines

APPLIES TO: qnfo-social (Bluesky, Mastodon, X, LinkedIn via Buffer). Effort S.

STATE 2026-10-26: qnfo-social/worker.js is under another session''s live claim (2026-10-26); the in-text marker is that file''s next change after the claim is released.

