INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at, predicate_id)
SELECT 'BP26-D1-DISCIPLINE-1: D1 discipline: indexed hot queries, batched transactional writes, Sessions API reads, Time Travel bookmark before every migration, quarterly restore drill', 'Charter pillar: core. BP26 best-practice catalogue item 2.2, top-20 rank 16 (research report wf-232b4527-680f-8492-8dc9-5ab6ae365e14 (2026-10-26); owner directive 2026-10-26).
Project BP26.ENGINEERING under program QNFO.INFRA (program-manager:QNFO.INFRA).

PRACTICE: Versioned migrations only; EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN on hot queries and queryEfficiency monitoring; db.batch() for multi-statement writes; chunk large UPDATE/DELETE (about 1,000 rows); Sessions API with bookmarks for read-heavy public pages; a Time Travel bookmark recorded before every migration; a restore drill every 90 days. Limits: 10 GB per database, 100 bound parameters, 100 KB per statement, 30 s per query or batch, single-threaded per database (qnfo-audit is about 0.9 GB and has hit SQLITE_NOMEM in fleet_tick).

SOURCES: D1 limits https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/platform/limits/; read replication https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/best-practices/read-replication/; indexes https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/best-practices/use-indexes/; Time Travel https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/reference/time-travel/

APPLIES TO: qnfo-audit, q08-signal, living-paper and every D1-backed Worker. Effort S-M.

METRICS (registered in metric_registry with triggers by migrations/2026-10-26-best-practice-catalogue.sql; each starts UNMEASURED and the producer that measures it is part of this issue):
- d1_db_size_pct: largest D1 database size / 10 GB (account D1 list); target <= 0.7.
- d1_restore_drill_age_days: days since the last successful Time Travel restore drill into a scratch database; target <= 90.
